{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfba3hEqsHKvf8A5i6CVW", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The tests use pytest, and the `Makefile` has two targets for running them.\n\n**1. Install the dependencies** (per `README.md`):\n```sh\npip install -e .[dev]\n```\n\n**2. Run the tests:**\n```sh\nmake test-fast   # runs: pytest -m \"not postgres\" -q   (skips the Postgres-marked tests)\nmake test        # runs: pytest -q                     (runs everything, including the Postgres tests)\n```\n\nFor day-to-day work, use `make test-fast`. It doesn't need a database.\n\n`make test` also runs the tests marked `postgres`, so it needs a Postgres instance to be reachable. A note saved in the project's memory store says to run `docker compose up db` first, but I couldn't find a compose file in the repo. That step may be out of date, or the database may be set up some other way. If you need the full suite, check how your environment provides Postgres."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 170, "cache_read_input_tokens": 21643, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 170}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "1467f044-7a2b-4065-993f-026454db978a", "uuid": "0738acc9-bf0c-4b94-8a8e-c6d836191c33", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:09:02.080Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfba3gu1FuQ2FkKDkjnRG"}
